+Compressed files
+----------------
+The ``read_*`` functions read a file compressed with gzip, bz2 or xz
+whatever its name: they recognise the compression by its first bytes. The
+``write_*`` functions take ``compression="gzip"``, ``"bz2"`` or ``"xz"`` to
+compress what they write, also into an open file; a file name ending in
+``.xz`` is compressed with xz, as ``.gz`` and ``.bz2`` are.
